    <h1>Child Safety & Anti-Exploitation Standards</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> March 27, 2026</p>

    <p>STRNGER is an anonymous social networking platform designed strictly for users aged <strong>18 and older</strong>. We are committed to providing a safe environment and have zero tolerance for the exploitation of minors.</p>

    <h2>1. Zero Tolerance Policy</h2>
    <p>STRNGER strictly prohibits the creation, upload, sharing, or promotion of Child Sexual Abuse Material (CSAM). Any account found engaging in such activity will be permanently banned immediately, and all relevant data will be preserved for law enforcement.</p>

    <h2>2. Prevention and Moderation</h2>
    <p>To prevent the exploitation of children, STRNGER employs the following measures:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Age Gating:</strong> All users must confirm they are 18+ before accessing the platform.</li>
        <li><strong>In-App Reporting:</strong> Users have access to a "Report" feature in every chat window and Community Circle to flag suspicious or illegal content.</li>
        <li><strong>Manual Review:</strong> Our moderation team prioritizes reports related to child safety for immediate review.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Cooperation with Law Enforcement</h2>
    <p>STRNGER complies with all regional and international laws regarding the reporting of child exploitation. We work with the National Center for Missing & Exploited Children (NCMEC) and other global authorities to report CSAM and assist in investigations.</p>

    <h2>4. Reporting a Violation</h2>
    <p>If you encounter content that violates these safety standards, please use the in-app reporting tools or contact our designated Safety Point of Contact immediately.</p>

